  "objects": [
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 21,
      "y": 3,
      "text": [
        "ROUTE 4. SALTHOLLOW BEHIND. TIDEGLASS 12, ALL OF IT DOWNHILL.",
        "Four shelves and three passes. Take the passes. The banks only go one way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 13,
      "text": [
        "THE HEADLAND. Stop here. Everyone does.",
        "That is the Caeloran Sea, and it is a very long way down, and you cannot get",
        "to it from here or from the next shelf or from the one after that."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 34,
      "y": 14,
      "text": [
        "A sea-mark: one stone, set upright, leaning where four hundred years of wind",
        "has pushed it. Vessels coming up the coast line it up with the beacon on the ridge.",
        "Somebody has been at the base of it recently with a theodolite and left the pegs in."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 22,
      "text": [
        "SALTHOLLOW PANS. Eleven. Filled on the spring tide, walled, and let go.",
        "Six weeks of sun and wind and what is left is what cures the hides on the shoulder",
        "and salts the fish in Tideglass. One coast, three trades, one puddle of water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 19,
      "text": [
        "Salt, barrelled and stacked, waiting for a cart that is late.",
        "The tally chalked on the end barrel has been rubbed out and rewritten twice.",
        "Under it, smaller: RIDGE ROAD FULL AGAIN. THIRD WEEK."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 12,
      "y": 28,
      "text": [
        "THE TIDELINE. Channels fill from the east on the turn, fast, and without a sound.",
        "What is a path at dawn is a channel by noon and a path again by dark.",
        "Under that, scratched: NINETY-FOUR DAYS. ASK THE WATCHER."
      ]
    },
